Subject: [PATCH 10/12] =?UTF-8?q?Big=20screen:=20transitions=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20everything=20rolls=20down=20onto=20the=20screen=20(or=20your?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20choice)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Whenever something comes onto the big screen — a deck, the lobby coming
back, the event background, an event view, a live poll, the video player —
it enters with the screen's chosen transition. Default ROLL DOWN, like a
projector screen unrolling: a metal roller bar rides the leading edge and the
screen settles with a little bounce. Also: roll up, curtain, iris, slide,
zoom, flip down, fade (exactly the old cross-fade), none (instant).

- hanns_screen_enter.js: watches the layers' on/off classes and plays the
  entrance with the Web Animations API; nothing about how a layer works
  changes. A deck over the lobby lifts the stage (see-through meanwhile) so
  it unrolls OVER the lobby, which stays up until the roll lands
- control board → Sources → "Screen transitions": nine choices, each
  previews itself on hover; "Preview on the big screen" replays it there
- server: look_for/set_look in ScreenStyle.settings["look"] (no migration),
  POST /screenart/s/<token>/look/, "look" in the screen state, a
  look_preview socket message
- prefers-reduced-motion on the projector → the plain fade
- test fix: test_video no longer races its own background conversion
